# DS-001 Development Standard
## Part 01 - Development Philosophy

Version: 1.0

Project: Pool OS

Date: 2026-07-03

---

# Purpose

This document defines the mandatory development standard for the Pool OS project.

This standard overrides Cursor default behavior.

Every RFC.

Every FIX.

Every Feature.

Every Refactor.

Every Bug Investigation.

Must follow this document.

---

# Primary Goal

The objective of Pool OS is NOT to produce code.

The objective is to produce

a stable,

maintainable,

professional

pool training application.

Code is only a tool.

Stability is the product.

---

# Development Philosophy

Priority order is fixed.

Cursor MUST always follow this order.

Priority 1

Correct Business Logic

↓

Priority 2

Application Stability

↓

Priority 3

Data Integrity

↓

Priority 4

Performance

↓

Priority 5

UI

↓

Priority 6

Code Beauty

Never sacrifice a higher priority to improve a lower priority.

---

# Project Principles

Pool OS follows these principles.

## Principle 1

Never redesign architecture during bug fixing.

Architecture changes are only allowed through RFC.

---

## Principle 2

Never implement new features while critical bugs still exist.

Priority

P0

must always be zero before feature development continues.

---

## Principle 3

One FIX

One Bug Group

A FIX must never solve multiple unrelated problems.

Example

GOOD

FIX-007A

Match

FIX-007B

Statistics

FIX-007C

Coach

BAD

FIX-007

Match

Statistics

Coach

Equipment

Player

---

## Principle 4

Small commits.

Small fixes.

Small regression risk.

Never perform large modifications.

---

## Principle 5

Every feature must have

Input

↓

Processing

↓

Storage

↓

Analysis

↓

Output

No isolated modules are allowed.

---

# Development Phases

Pool OS development consists of the following phases.

Phase 1

Architecture

↓

Phase 2

RFC Implementation

↓

Phase 3

Stabilization

↓

Phase 4

APK Build

↓

Phase 5

User Acceptance Test

↓

Phase 6

Bug Fix

↓

Phase 7

Beta Release

↓

Phase 8

Production

Cursor must always know the current phase.

Different phases require different behavior.

---

# Current Project Phase

Current phase is

USER ACCEPTANCE TEST

Therefore

Cursor MUST

Fix bugs only.

Cursor MUST NOT

Create new features.

Refactor architecture.

Optimize code.

Improve UI without request.

---

# Core Rule

Whenever a conflict occurs

between

adding a feature

or

fixing stability

Cursor must always choose

stability.

---

End of Part 01

