## Part 03 - Bug Analysis Standard

Version: 1.0

Project: Pool OS

Date: 2026-07-03

---

# Purpose

This document defines the mandatory bug investigation process.

Pool OS does not allow speculative debugging.

Every bug must be investigated before implementation.

A FIX is NOT allowed until the Root Cause has been confirmed.

---

# Golden Rule

Never fix a symptom.

Always fix the Root Cause.

---

# Bug Investigation Workflow

Every bug must follow the same sequence.

User Report

↓

Reproduce

↓

Execution Trace

↓

Root Cause

↓

Impact Analysis

↓

Fix Strategy

↓

Regression Analysis

↓

Implementation

↓

Validation

Skipping any step is prohibited.

---

# Step 1

User Report

Collect only facts.

Never assume.

Example

GOOD

User presses Win.

Screen becomes gray.

No further interaction.

BAD

Probably dialog problem.

Maybe Provider issue.

---

# Step 2

Reproduce

Cursor must reproduce the issue.

If reproduction fails

Cursor must report

Unable to Reproduce.

Never continue by guessing.

---

# Step 3

Execution Trace

Cursor must trace the complete execution path.

Every bug investigation must contain

UI

↓

Event

↓

State

↓

Provider

↓

Repository

↓

Database

↓

Return

↓

State Update

↓

UI Refresh

No step may be omitted.

---

# Example

Button

↓

onPressed()

↓

Provider.recordRack()

↓

Repository.saveRack()

↓

Database.insert()

↓

Provider.refresh()

↓

UI rebuild()

If execution stops

the exact location must be identified.

---

# Step 4

Root Cause

Root Cause must be classified.

Confirmed

Not Confirmed

Need Runtime Trace

Only Confirmed Root Cause may enter implementation.

---

# Root Cause Rules

Cursor must NEVER use uncertain language.

The following words are prohibited.

Maybe

Probably

Likely

Seems

Possible

Might

Appears to

Looks like

Instead

Cursor must write

Confirmed

Not Confirmed

Need Runtime Trace

---

# Incorrect Example

Probably Provider failed.

---

Correct Example

Execution stopped inside

recordRack()

because

Provider state changed after dialog disposal.

Root Cause Confirmed.

---

# Step 5

Impact Analysis

Every bug must define impact.

Only one level.

P0

Application unusable

Crash

Data corruption

Wrong business logic

No workaround

P1

Feature incorrect

Wrong statistics

Wrong Coach advice

Calculation error

P2

UI

Localization

Alignment

Display

P3

Improvement

UX

Animation

Enhancement

---

# Step 6

Affected Modules

Every bug must identify

all affected modules.

Example

Match

Rack

Coach

Dashboard

Statistics

Equipment

Player

Daily Readiness

Session

Navigation

Database

---

# Step 7

Regression Risk

Every fix must estimate

LOW

MEDIUM

HIGH

with explanation.

Example

LOW

Provider refresh only.

No database changes.

HIGH

Database migration required.

Statistics recalculated.

---

# Step 8

Fix Strategy

Implementation is NOT code.

Implementation is only the strategy.

Example

GOOD

Replace invalid dialog context.

Keep Provider unchanged.

No database modification.

BAD

Rewrite Match module.

---

# Step 9

Validation

Every bug must include

Verification Steps.

Example

Press Win.

Rack Summary opens.

Save Rack.

Return to Match.

Continue next Rack.

No gray screen.

---

# Bug Analysis Output

Every BUG_ANALYSIS.md must contain

Bug ID

Priority

User Symptoms

Reproduction

Execution Trace

Root Cause

Affected Modules

Affected Files

Fix Strategy

Regression Risk

Validation Steps

Acceptance Criteria

No additional sections are allowed.

---

# Runtime Trace

If Root Cause cannot be confirmed

Cursor must stop implementation.

Cursor must request

Runtime Trace.

Runtime Trace may include

Debug Log

Stack Trace

Exception

Provider State

Database Query

Navigation Stack

No implementation is allowed before Root Cause becomes Confirmed.

---

# Mandatory Rule

Bug Fixing is an engineering process.

Bug Fixing is NOT trial-and-error.

Cursor must never implement changes simply because they "might work."

Every implementation must be supported by confirmed evidence.

---

End of Part 03

# DS-001 Development Standard
## Part 04 - Root Cause Analysis

Version: 1.0

Project: Pool OS

Date: 2026-07-03

---

# Purpose

This document defines how Root Cause Analysis (RCA) must be performed.

Root Cause Analysis is mandatory before every FIX.

No implementation may begin until Root Cause has been confirmed.

---

# Definition

Root Cause

=

The first defect that directly causes the observed problem.

Root Cause

≠

The place where the application crashes.

---

# Example

User presses Win.

↓

Dialog disappears.

↓

Gray screen.

The crash location

Navigator.pop()

is NOT necessarily the Root Cause.

The Root Cause may be

Provider disposed

before

Navigator.pop().

Always search for the first incorrect state.

---

# Five Levels of Analysis

Every investigation must move through these levels.

Level 1

User Symptom

↓

Level 2

Application Behavior

↓

Level 3

Execution Flow

↓

Level 4

Data Flow

↓

Level 5

Root Cause

Never stop before Level 5.

---

# Level 1

User Symptom

Describe only observable facts.

Example

User presses Save.

Application freezes.

No SnackBar.

No navigation.

No assumptions.

---

# Level 2

Application Behavior

Describe what actually happened.

Example

Dialog remained visible.

State changed.

No rebuild occurred.

Repository never executed.

---

# Level 3

Execution Flow

Trace every function.

Example

Button

↓

onPressed()

↓

Provider.save()

↓

Repository.insert()

↓

Database

↓

Provider.refresh()

↓

UI rebuild()

Locate exactly where execution stopped.

---

# Level 4

Data Flow

Track every important object.

Example

Match

↓

Rack

↓

Repository

↓

SQLite

↓

Repository

↓

Provider

↓

State

↓

Widget

Never assume the object still exists.

Always verify.

---

# Level 5

Root Cause

Only one Root Cause is allowed.

Example

GOOD

Dialog Context became invalid after await.

BAD

Provider

Database

Navigator

Maybe Riverpod

---

# Root Cause Categories

Every Root Cause belongs to exactly one category.

Navigation

State Management

Database

Business Logic

Async

UI

Dependency Injection

Localization

Performance

Memory

Configuration

Unknown

---

# Flutter Specific Analysis

For Flutter applications,

Root Cause investigation must always verify

Widget Lifecycle

↓

Build()

↓

State

↓

Provider

↓

Repository

↓

Database

↓

Navigation

---

# Navigation Checklist

Always verify

Navigator

GoRouter

Dialog

BottomSheet

showDialog()

showModalBottomSheet()

context.pop()

context.go()

